            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Generally no. Storm drains in most areas flow directly to streams and lakes without treatment, and many local codes prohibit washing automotive fluids or degreaser residue into them. Rinse onto gravel or lawn where allowed, or collect wash water with a wet vacuum and dispose of it through your local household hazardous waste program."
          }
