          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "On concrete, often yes. Spot degreasing can leave a noticeably lighter patch because it removes years of general grime along with the oil. A whole-surface wash with a driveway cleaner and a surface cleaner attachment evens the color. On asphalt, sealing the driveway after spot cleaning does the same job and protects the surface."
          }
        }
